ith embedded content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Tries to estimate the users' bandwidth on pages with integrated YouTube videos. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie YSC Registers a unique ID to keep statistics of what videos from YouTube the user has seen. Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie Unclassified 7 Unclassified cookies are cookies that we are in the process of classifying, together with the providers of individual cookies. LinkedIn 1 Learn more about this provider li_fat_id Pending Maximum Storage Duration : 30 days Type : HTTP Cookie Tu/e 3 Learn more about this provider aff_2577a2901 Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie aff_93e95bd6a Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie page_view_count Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTML Local Storage YouTube 3 Learn more about this provider PersistentEntityStoreDb:V34421bd5||#EntityAssociationStore Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB PersistentEntityStoreDb:V34421bd5||#EntityStore Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB yt-player-caption-persistence Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage Cross-domain consent [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS_COUNT#] [#BULK_CONSENT_TITLE#] List of domains your consent applies to: [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS#] Cookie declaration last updated on 8/27/26 by Cookiebot [#IABV2_TITLE#] [#IABV2_BODY_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_LEGITIMATE_INTEREST_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PREFERENCE_INTRO#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies EngD in Designing Hu... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies EngD in Designing Human-System Interaction Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Engineering Doctorate (EngD) Organisation: Department of Industrial Design Apply no later than: 18-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.173 - € 3.173 Apply now Introduction Within the MEDAL project (Motivating mEaningful Daily Data collection through Design, AI, and SociaL engagement, https://www.clicknl.nl/en/ontwerpkrachtentransities/medal/ ), TU/e leads a consortium — including Catharina Hospital, Fashion Tech Farm, and other creative and knowledge partners like Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences — investigating how personal life data, alongside clinical measurements, can find a place in cardiovascular care pathways. The recurring tension here: patients at home need data that is both clinically usable and effortless to fit into daily life. This EngD track works out that tension specifically for the heart failure care pathway. Job Description Assignment You research and design how contextual data - living patterns, activity, emotional and social signals - can be used alongside physiological measurements to support heart failure patients in self-management at home. Co-design workshops with heart failure patients and healthcare professionals at Catharina Hospital to identify data needs and interaction preferences. You can work with the team in the hospital who already redesigned and develop the care pathway. Translate these insights into design requirements for data collection, visualization, and feedback. Collaborate with Fashion Tech Farm on a tangible, textile-based exploration of what this health data can feel like — a more explorative, conceptual counterpart to the functional prototype, probing wearable and material forms of data experience beyond screens and numbers. Develop and iterate a data-driven prototype for home monitoring, working with technology partners like Cardiron. Run real-world pilot tests on subjects like usability, clinical relevance, user engagement, and impact on home-based self-management. Outcome A validated prototype, embedded in the existing systems in the hospital for participatory home care for heart failure patients, alongside a textile/tangible design exploration developed with Fashion Tech Farm that opens up alternative, more embodied forms of engaging with health data. Together these feed the design principles contributed to the broader MEDAL framework for data interaction in participatory healthcare. Job Requirements A relevant Master's degree, in an area related to the fields of industrial design, human-computer interaction, or comparable. Affinity with healthcare contexts and working with patients and clinicians. Experience with co-design and prototyping; interest in material/tangible design or wearables is a plus. To be successful in Dutch Healthcare context, to engage with healthcare professionals and patients, speaking Dutch is a preference. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Full-time employment for 2 years. Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale TOIO (€ 3.173 gross per month (full-time)). In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. High-quality training programs on general skills, didactics and topics related to research and valorization. An excellent technical infrastructure, and on-campus children's day care. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Partially paid parental leave and an allowance for commuting, working from home and internet costs. A TU/e Postdoc Association that helps you to build a stronger and broader academic and personal network, and offe"
    },
