V2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies University Teacher D... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies University Teacher Data Analytics and AI (Full-time or Part-time) Personal type: Scientific staff Field of expertise: Other academic staff Organisation: Department of Industrial Engineering & Innovation Sciences Apply no later than: 18-10-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.706 - € 6.682 Apply now Introduction Do you enjoy inspiring the next generation of professionals? Are you enthusiastic about data analytics and AI? We are looking for a university teacher to develop and teach courses on data analytics and AI, possibly next to a job, PhD, or Post-doc position they are already fulfilling. Job Description We are seeking a University Teacher to teach courses in data analytics and AI and to supervise student projects, including bachelor’s and master’s thesis projects. Teaching responsibilities include developing and continuously updating course materials based on the latest scientific advances. This is especially important in the rapidly evolving fields of data analytics and AI, because courses must incorporate up-to-date AI methods, tools, and techniques. At the same time, students need to develop the skills to use AI responsibly and effectively as part of their learning process. You will play a key role in equipping students with both a strong theoretical foundation and the practical competencies to do this. The position is based in the Information Systems group, in the Industrial Engineering and Innovation Sciences (IE&IS) department at Eindhoven University of Technology. You will be working with our professors, PhD students, and teaching assistants to deliver high-quality education. The Information Systems group develops methods, tools, and techniques that support the entire lifecycle of Information Systems development, including advanced analytics and AI. It focuses on leveraging data analytics and AI to enhance organizational decision-making. Applications across various sectors are studied, with a focus on healthcare, transportation and logistics, services, smart industry, mobility, and energy. As a member of the group, you will contribute to teaching students how to improve organizational decision making with data science and AI. In this role, you will be responsible for developing and delivering high-quality course materials, teaching lectures and tutorials, designing assignments and exams, and supervising student projects, including bachelor’s and master’s thesis projects. In addition, 20% of your time will be dedicated to education-related research. The position is initially offered for a period of six months on a full-time basis or up to twelve months on a part-time basis. The appointment can be combined with another part-time position, such as a role at another institution or an existing PhD or postdoctoral appointment at TU/e. Depending on performance and available funding, there may be opportunities to extend the appointment or move to a permanent position. This position offers a unique opportunity to contribute to the education of the next generation of data analytics and AI professionals, while helping shape the future of AI education at the university. Job Requirements The successful candidate will meet most of the following requirements: You have a Master's or PhD degree in Data Science, AI, Computer Science, Industrial Engineering, or a similar field of study. You possess strong programming skills, preferably in Python, and are comfortable applying them in data analytics and AI contexts. You have a strong interest in education and some prior teaching experience, for example as a teaching assistant. You enjoy collaborating in (teaching) teams. Your communication skills are excellent as is your proficiency in English and your ability to collaborate in an international setting. Experience with the Dutch or broader European higher education system is considered a strong advantage. The preferred starting date is January 1, 2027. A later date by up to 2 months is negotiable, but not preferred. Conditions of Employment A meaningful job in a dynamic and ambitious university, in an interdisciplinary setting and within an international network. You will work on a beautiful, green campus within walking distance of the central train station. In addition, we offer you: Salary in accordance with"
    }
  },
